-- title:
--   Degree reduction for the naive height on J₀(N)
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \ge 1$ and a finite extension $K$ of $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, realised as an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ that is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}$. Work with the field $F_N$ obtained by adjoining to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((t))$, the coefficientwise images of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((t))$ generated by the divisor expansions attached to $N$, and with $J_0(N) = \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of $F_N$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, i.e. degree-zero divisors on the places of $F_N$ modulo principal ones. Let $g' \in \mathbb{N}$ satisfy the Riemann-type hypothesis $h_R$: every divisor $D$ on $F_N$ with $\deg D \ge g'$ admits a nonzero $f \in F_N$ with $D(v) + \mathrm{ord}_v(f) \ge 0$ at every place $v$, that is, $D$ is linearly equivalent to an effective divisor. Let $g'' \ge g'$. The conclusion asserts the existence of real constants $R \ge 0$ and $C$ such that for every class $x$ in the fixed points of $J_0(N)$ under the subgroup of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ fixing $K$, one has $h_{g'}(x) \le R\,h_{g''}(x) + C$, where $h_g(x)$ is the infimum of $\mathrm{divNaiveHeight}$ over those Galois-stable effective divisors of the shape $E + g\cdot(\infty)$, with $E$ of degree zero representing $x$.
--
--   This is the degree-comparison ("cheap representative") step in the height machinery on $J_0(N)$: passing from representatives supported with multiplicity $g''$ at the cusp to representatives with multiplicity $g'$ costs at most an affine amount. It is used in the descent argument [`ModularCurve.JZero.naiveHeight_descent_of_prime_of_five_le`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZero.naiveHeight_descent_of_prime_of_five_le).
